xt-cluster-shm
==============

Tiny AGL Cluster IC stand-in that renders a speedometer + tripmeter
into a wl_shm buffer with cairo. No EGL, no V3D — runs on whatever
weston backend is up.

Why this exists
---------------

This renders through wl_shm only, with no GPU involvement, which makes it
useful for bringing a display path up before the V3D stack is known good and
for telling a compositor problem apart from a GPU problem.

It was written for a configuration in which every EGL/GLES client
(weston-simple-egl, kmscube, SurfaceFlinger via virglrenderer) showed a
transparent black window: vc4_hvs could not take the HVS core clock while the
firmware display driver still held it. The shipping configuration no longer
has that problem -- weston runs gl-renderer through Mesa V3D -- so treat this
as a diagnostic tool. Note also that cluster-service from
packagegroup-agl-ic-core is a backend-only service and renders nothing itself.

xt-cluster-shm proves the wayland surface chain is alive end-to-end
and gives the demo a recognisable Cluster IC face on HDMI without
touching V3D.

Boot path
---------

  weston.socket (/run/wayland-0)
    -> weston.service, whose weston.socket publishes /run/wayland-0
       -> xt-cluster-shm.service
          -> wayland xdg_shell + wl_shm
             -> desktop-shell.so places it at the centre / fullscreens it
                -> HDMI scanout via the firmware display driver

Diagnostics
-----------

  systemctl status xt-cluster-shm
  journalctl -u xt-cluster-shm -b
  pidof xt-cluster-shm                   # client alive
  ls -la /run/wayland-0                  # socket present
  ssh root@192.168.10.10 \
    'XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run WAYLAND_DISPLAY=wayland-0 xt-cluster-shm'  # foreground

If you would rather use a GPU-backed cluster
--------------------------------------------

This recipe is a fallback. The real Cluster IC (packagegroup-agl-ic-core
+ cluster_service + the GUI binary that pulls in
qtquickcontrols2-agl / agl-image-flutter) needs working EGL, which
needs the firmware-mailbox passthrough fix in meta-xt-rpi5's domd DT.

